1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,367
Habitat Health Monitor.

2
00:00:01,467 --> 00:00:03,400
A camera tracks every lift on the bench

3
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:05,933
and converts each rep into work, in joules.

4
00:00:06,033 --> 00:00:09,067
An Arduino UNO senses cabin air and sounds the alarm;

5
00:00:09,167 --> 00:00:11,033
a NodeMCU reports the weight's tilt.

6
00:00:11,133 --> 00:00:15,333
A Raspberry Pi hub checks every reading against NASA limits, with no link to Earth.

7
00:00:15,433 --> 00:00:18,867
The crew panel adds food energy, training work and body mass.

8
00:00:18,967 --> 00:00:22,167
Cabin temperature and humidity are scored on NASA's own bands.

9
00:00:22,267 --> 00:00:26,233
Mission control sees it all twelve minutes later, over a simulated Mars link.

10
00:00:26,333 --> 00:00:28,900
An educational prototype, not a medical device.
